sentences.l:
Nor again did Hector allow the manly Trojans, either,
to sleep, but together he kept summoning all the best,
as many as were of the Trojans leaders and lords;

Now there was among the Trojans one Dolon, Eumedes’ son,
of a divine herald, rich in gold, rich in bronze,
who in form, indeed, was bad, but fleet-footed;

But when they were away as far as a spear-cast or even less,
he knew them for hostile men, and his quick knees he set moving
to flee;
